  "limits": [
    "This is one pinned default renderer connection-race observation, not a universal delay value or a proprietary request producer.",
    "The444ms logged delay is not hardcoded into Dart. Public Chromium computes delay from network QUIC history, recently-broken state, server SRTT and feature inputs, capped by the controller.",
    "The public source is read, not decompiled. Its exact active feature/network-history/SRTT inputs are not recovered by this artifact.",
    "One H2 send per request is observed before QUIC handshake completion; the still-opening alternative is not a replay of the HTTP body.",
    "No original session/profile import, application, account or network runs. Request headers/body, credentials and account/device/content identifiers are not exported; protocol source IDs remain explicit.",
    "Dart now races transport preparation before request dispatch. The local peer proves H2 winners, later H3 use and no duplicate HTTP request; it does not reproduce these exact original network-history/SRTT inputs.",
    "Dart uses pinned public macOS defaults: no extra feature delay, no delay with an available H2 session, otherwise1.5*SRTT or300ms fallback capped at3s after observed QUIC success. Persisted network history, active feature overrides, network-change detection and complete broken-alternative backoff remain unproved."
